00:06:04.290 --> 00:06:11.400
 Well, that's a really good place to start because it looks so many different ways,

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:16.520
 right? And it sounds like, to me, when looking over your work, a lot of what it's about is

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:24.380
 these negotiations of what that impact has been on cities over time and what people imagine from

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:31.330
 those spaces, I guess. So could you talk a little bit about what you think those impacts are or give

00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:33.810
 a few examples of different ways that's looked?

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:42.560
 Mm-hmm. Urban agriculture really appeals to me on a deep level in a way that I've maintained a connection

